  "gaps": [
    "The capture labels the professional block 'Professional Courses (66 credits)', but it lists only 16 professional courses at 3 credits each, which is 48 credits. The capture does not reconcile this 18-credit difference.",
    "The printed block totals (66 + 42 + 30 = 138) do not match the stated 120 total credits. The listed courses (48 professional + 42 general education + 30 general electives) do sum to 120.",
    "No catalog year/term is stated. The only dated reference is the tuition schedule 'Fall '26 - Summer '27'.",
    "No residency or institutional-completion requirement is stated. The page says only that 'CCO accepts up to 90 transfer credits toward a bachelor's degree'.",
    "The capture does not say whether a course listed in more than one general education category (e.g., COMM 130, COMM 140, CRIT 220, PHIL 240, MKCM 120) can satisfy more than one requirement.",
    "The General Education Elective is limited to 'Any ARTS, COMM, CRIT, ECON, ENGL, HIST, MATH, PHIL, PSYC, SCIE, SOCI, MKCM 120, CRIM except CRIM-225'. No specific course list or credit-level restrictions are given beyond that.",
    "No minimum graduation GPA, upper-level credit minimum, or grade requirements for major courses are stated.",
    "Prerequisites noted but not ledger items: SOCI 350 requires SOCI-110, and HCMT 490 requires 'Complete 108 credits'."
  ],
